<component type="desktop">
  <id>io.github.grxtor.Kite</id>
  <name>Kite</name>
  <summary>Custom Minecraft Launcher to easily manage multiple Minecraft installations at once</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.grxtor">
    <name>grxtor</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>Apache-2.0</project_license>
  <description>
    <p>Kite is a custom launcher for Minecraft that focuses on predictability, long term stability and simplicity. With MMCO Plugin system.</p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Easily install game modifications, such as Fabric, Forge, NeoForge and Quilt</li>
      <li>Easily install and update modpacks from the Kite</li>
      <li>Control your Java settings</li>
      <li>Ability to install MMCO plugin from outside</li>
      <li>Ability to use proprietary plugins signed with MMCS.</li>
      <li>Manage worlds and resource packs from the launcher</li>
      <li>See logs and other details easily through a dashboard</li>
      <li>Kill Minecraft in case of a crash/freeze</li>
      <li>Ability to disable MMCO plugins you don't want.</li>
      <li>Isolate Minecraft instances to keep everything clean</li>
      <li>Install and update mods directly from the launcher</li>
      <li>Customize the launcher with themes, and more</li>
      <li>And cats :3</li>
      <li>With more themes, UwU</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <recommends>
    <memory>2048</memory>
  </recommends>
  <releases>
    <release version="1.2.0" date="2026-10-30">
      <description>
        <p>Looks, the friends panel and a choice of graphics API.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Looks: Sahne, Sade and Gece beside Klasik, picked in Settings with a preview of each one's Home.</li>
          <li>Friends panel on every page: a strip of heads at the window's right edge that opens into the full list, with Join.</li>
          <li>Kite Performance: Vulkan or OpenGL for Minecraft 26.2 and later.</li>
          <li>New instance: the type beside the version, and Kite Performance's mods picked one by one.</li>
          <li>macOS: the title bar is part of Kite's top bar, and the disk image opens on Kite's sky and asks to agree to the licence.</li>
          <li>A Microsoft account without a refresh token asks for a new sign-in.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.1.0" date="2026-10-26">
      <description>
        <p>Kite Performance, friends and the Kite mod.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Kite Performance: per-instance performance mods installed at Play, and Speed up for vanilla instances.</li>
          <li>Friends: see which server your friends are on and join them.</li>
          <li>The Kite mod for Minecraft 26.3: an in-game menu, a HUD editor, HUD modules and in-game friends.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.0" date="2026-10-24">
      <description>
        <p>First Kite release, forked from MeshMC 11.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
  <categories>
    <category>Game</category>
  </categories>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/grxtor/kite</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/grxtor/kite/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/grxtor/kite</url>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1">
    <content_attribute id="violence-fantasy">moderate</content_attribute>
    <content_attribute id="social-chat">intense</content_attribute>
  </content_rating>
  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#3584e4</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#0a2d6f</color>
  </branding>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">@Kite_AppID@.desktop</launchable>
</component>
